# Counterexample for fix bond/react's "assigned_count == nfirst_neighs" GUESSFAIL
# check in make_a_guess() (fix_bond_react.cpp, ~line 1586).
#
# System: one single coarse-grained homopolymer chain (13 beads, all same type).
# Beads 5 and 9 sit 1.0 apart in SPACE but only 4 bonds apart on the BACKBONE.
# The reaction template is two disconnected 7-atom fragments (bonding atom = the
# middle, 4th, atom of each), meant to model an intermolecular crosslink between
# two DIFFERENT chains. Because 5 and 9 are so close along the same backbone,
# the two fragments' outward (radius-3) neighbor searches physically overlap on
# beads 6, 7, 8 -- a pseudo-intrachain match that is topologically impossible to
# fill (the same real atom would have to be two different template atoms).
#
# Expected WITH the check (as shipped): a clean reject. No reaction happens,
# no error. Thermo will show 0 reactions.
#
# Expected WITHOUT the check (comment out the line noted above and rebuild):
# a template slot is left permanently unfilled, the same pioneer is reselected
# every pass, and the run dies with:
#   "Fix bond/react: Excessive iteration of superimpose algorithm."

units       lj
dimension   3
boundary    p p p
atom_style  molecular

read_data   data.chain extra/special/per/atom 30 extra/bond/per/atom 2

pair_style  zero 2.0
pair_coeff  * *

bond_style  zero
bond_coeff  *

special_bonds lj 0.0 0.0 0.0

velocity    all set 0.0 0.0 0.0

molecule    pre_mol  pre.mol
molecule    post_mol post.mol

fix         rxn all bond/react react wefail1_test all 1 0.0 1.5 pre_mol post_mol map.txt

thermo_style custom step f_rxn[1]
thermo      1

timestep    1.0
run         100
